<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nicobar Islands</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Nicobar Islands are an archipelago in the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a>, today part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>'s union territory of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andaman-and-nicobar-islands">Andaman and Nicobar Islands</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> claimed them from the 18th century and made several failed attempts at settlement before giving up the claim in 1868-1869. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> handed them nominally to Azad Hind.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nicobar-islands.jpg" alt="Nicobar Islands" width="320" height="219" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: edited by M.Minderhoud · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nicobar_Islands.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
